# <%= it.title %> MCP server

MCP server for **<%= it.title %> <%= it.version %>**, generated by [make-mcp](https://github.com/make-mcp/make-mcp) on <%= it.generatedAt %>.

<% if (it.docs) { %>
## Documentation tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `search_docs` | Full-text search across <%= it.docs.pageCount %> pages |
| `get_page` | Full Markdown of a page |
| `list_topics` | All pages grouped by section |
<% if (it.docs.componentCount) { %>| `get_component` | One of <%= it.docs.componentCount %> components with class names and examples |
<% } %>

Every page is also available as resource `docs://<%= it.name %>/{path}`.

**Source:** <% for (const s of it.docs.sources) { %><%= s.url %><% if (s.ref) { %> @ <%= s.ref %><% } %> <% } %>  
**License of the documentation:** <%= it.license || "unknown" %>.
<% if (it.docs.contentMode === "embedded") { %>
The documentation is embedded under `data/corpus.json` with attribution to its authors as permitted by its license.
<% } else { %>
The documentation is **not** included in this package. It is downloaded from the original source on your machine
(`npm run refresh` / `uv run server.py --refresh`) and cached under `~/.cache/make-mcp/`. Do not redistribute the cache.
<% } %>
<% } %>
<% if (it.api) { %>
## API tools

<%= it.api.endpointCount %> operations of **<%= it.api.title %>** (`<%= it.api.baseUrl %>`), one tool per operation.
Side-effect-free GET operations are additionally exposed as resources (`api://<%= it.name %>/…`).

### Configuration

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
<% for (const v of it.envVars) { %>| `<%= v.name %>` | <%= v.description %> |
<% } %>
Copy `.env.example` to `.env` or pass the variables via your MCP client configuration.
<% } %>
